**Theorem 8.1 (same-law operational transfer of the criterion).** Under
Assumptions 1.1 and 2.2, every finite law produced by a coordinate
face or the interpolation (FC.18), after the compatible merges,
has a common original optimal realization at its own request
$s=s_0r/\sqrt\alpha$, with the exact complete original outputs,
sharp joint cost and entire-fibre activity bound. For every integer
$m\ge0$ and every $r\in[r_-,r_+]$,

$$
\begin{gathered}
\mathcal T(s,t)=\frac{H_0+y\cdot B-\lambda r}{2},\qquad
n_{\rm tot}(s,t)=1+n_t(r),\\
n_{\rm tot}(s,t)\le m+1\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad r\in U_m,\\
n_{\rm tot}(s,t)=9\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad r\in U_8\setminus U_7,
\qquad
n_{\rm tot}(s,t)=10\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad r\notin U_8.
\end{gathered}
\tag{FC.24}
$$

The last equivalence is restricted to $r\in[r_-,r_+]$. If the
interval is nontrivial, its physical height slope is
$-\lambda\sqrt\alpha/(2s_0)$. There is no assertion of a slope
on an open interval when $r_-=r_+$.

